Port of the prototype from discussion pingdotgg/t3code#31476
(imqdee/t3code@46acd51f8e, branch feat/terminal-other-environment).

Behaviours:
- The drawer's New Terminal button gets a chevron menu "New terminal on" (the
  chevron's accessible name is "New Terminal on…") when the client knows more
  than one environment. The thread's machine is listed first ("This thread"),
  then the others by label. Entries are disabled with a reason: "Not
  connected", "Connecting" or "No terminal access" (no terminal:operate
  grant). The plain "+" still opens on the thread's machine.
- A terminal opened on another machine runs under the thread's id there. Its
  tab shows that machine's label. Splits from it open on the same machine and
  in the same folder. Writes, permissions and closes go to that machine. A
  link printed in it opens in the browser, because the thread's preview runs
  on the thread's machine.
- The starting folder is the thread's folder when it exists on the target
  (checked through file metadata, needs filesystem:read), else the target
  server's own cwd.
- Remote tabs persist in the client's terminal UI store and stay while the
  machine is offline.
- Closing a remote tab, or archiving or deleting the thread from this client,
  closes the remote session. The close is queued in persisted state first and
  RemoteTerminalCloseCoordinator retries it when the machine regains the
  terminal grant; queued closes for machines removed from the client are
  dropped.
- Deleting a thread this client does not hold (an archived thread, the
  unresolved delete branch) closes the thread's remote terminals after a
  successful delete, as archive and the resolved delete branch do, before the
  thread's terminal UI state is cleared. A failed delete leaves them alone.
- Removing a project or checkout from project settings closes the remote
  terminals of every loaded thread of each removed member, after that member's
  delete succeeded and its removal landed.
- A remote terminal open that fails queues a close for that exact session
  (target environment, thread id, terminal id) before its tab is removed, so a
  session the target created before failing is ended. Closing an unknown
  session is a no-op success on the server, so the queued close drains.
- terminal.open / terminal.attach accept an optional originEnvironmentId; the
  server keeps it on the session and returns it in TerminalSummary. A thread's
  known terminal sessions skip summaries whose origin is another environment.
  Servers without this field ignore it.

Integration details:
- Upstream #31857 (stopOnSettle) touched the same contracts; both fields are
  kept.
- Upstream moved the root route's hosts into an appHosts block that also
  mounts on /welcome; RemoteTerminalCloseCoordinator sits in that block next
  to ProjectCloneToastCoordinator.
- Upstream #29164 clears the terminal UI state after deleting a thread this
  client does not hold; the remote terminals are closed just before that, as
  in the resolved delete branch, because clearing the UI state drops the
  remote tabs.

Port to e07585e5fb:
- Manager.test.ts: the contracts import adds EnvironmentId and TerminalSummary next to upstream's new ProjectId, ThreadId and TerminalCwdNotFoundError.

Port to ee4ef06469:
- __root.tsx: RemoteTerminalCloseCoordinator mounts next to upstream's new ConnectDeviceApprovalCoordinator (#36419). useThreadTerminalActions.ts: the remote-terminal store imports sit next to upstream's closing-terminal hold (#29654), which guards same-machine closes; remote closes keep their persisted queue.

